> Oh yeh, I was trying to say "Sam, who is my friend, is a dog.". Would
> "le la sam pendo mi ku gerku" work?

No. LE doesn't accept bridi.

la .sam. noi pendo mi
          ^ noi is the key word here.

NOI attaches a subordinate bridi to a sumti in order to provide more
information about it. In the above example, "Sam, who is my
friend, ...". So {la .sam. noi pendo mi ku'o gerku} is what you want.

xorxes: no'i ca ma mi xusra lo du'u lo nu la .sam. pendo mi kei ku
gerku

